---
import './benefits.css';
import {placementSteps} from './placement.mjs';
---
<figure class="benefit-figure" data-benefit-placement>
  <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 4</span>Which requests can share a fill?</div>
  <div class="scene">
    <label>Copy lives <select data-placement><option value="local">Inside each process</option><option value="shared">In one shared cache</option></select></label>
    <p><strong data-clock data-live>Before requests</strong></p>
    <div class="stats"><span><strong data-reads data-live>0</strong> source reads</span><span><strong data-lookups data-live>0</strong> remote cache lookups</span></div>
    <div class="apps">
      <div class="box"><strong>App A</strong><span data-a data-live>Local copy: Empty</span></div>
      <div class="box"><strong>App B</strong><span data-b data-live>Local copy: Empty</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="shared-store" data-shared-panel hidden><div class="network">A ↘ network lookups ↙ B</div><div class="box used"><strong>Shared cache</strong><span data-shared data-live>Empty</span></div></div>
    <div class="source-store"><div class="network">On a miss: the requesting app reads the source</div><div class="box"><strong>Authoritative source</strong><span data-source data-live>GBP 20.00 · revision 1</span></div></div>
    <p class="callout" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Both processes start with an empty local cache. Neither can reuse the other’s memory.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 6</span><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
  <figcaption>One invented history, two placements. Every request uses <code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP</code>. Entries expire 30 seconds after insertion. Fills are immediate and sequential; no eviction, invalidation, failure or replica lag is modelled. The source change is the same in both runs. Cache fills also cross the network in the shared design; the counter counts lookup calls only.</figcaption>
  <details><summary>Both histories, as text</summary><ol>{placementSteps.map(step=><li><strong>{step.time}.</strong> Local: {step.localText} Shared: {step.sharedText}</li>)}</ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
  import {placementSteps} from './placement.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-benefit-placement]').forEach(root=>{
    const choice=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-placement]')!;
    const set=(selector:string,value:string|number)=>{root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent=String(value);};
    const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>placementSteps.length,draw:(index:number)=>{
      const step=placementSteps[index], shared=choice.value==='shared';
      set('[data-clock]',step.time);set('[data-reads]',step.reads[shared?1:0]);set('[data-lookups]',shared?step.lookups:0);
      set('[data-a]',shared?'No local copy':`Local copy: ${step.local[0]}`);set('[data-b]',shared?'No local copy':`Local copy: ${step.local[1]}`);
      set('[data-shared]',step.shared);set('[data-source]',step.source);set('[data-explanation]',shared?step.sharedText:step.localText);
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-shared-panel]')!.hidden=!shared;
    }});
    choice.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
  });
</script>
<style>
 .apps { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.75rem;margin-top:1rem; }
 .network { text-align:center;color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.8rem;padding:.6rem 0; }
 .shared-store .box,.source-store .box { text-align:center; }
 .source-store { margin-top:.5rem; }
 @media(max-width:540px) { .apps { gap:.4rem; } .apps .box { padding:.5rem; } }
</style>
